        ],
        "description": "Searches YouTube Music (InnerTube) and plays the m4a stream it resolves with yt-dlp. Gives the song's album art from InnerTube (`yt3`/`lh3.googleusercontent.com`). The engine installs yt-dlp: it downloads this platform's self-contained binary and verifies its hash (D-069); no Python is needed on the system. If a `cookies` secret is given, it's passed to yt-dlp as a cookie file — YouTube puts up a bot wall for data centre addresses (D-061). NOTE — yt-dlp isn't a script the engine jails but a separate program: its network traffic isn't limited by this plugin's permission list. There's no single-file release for Linux armv7 (`linux-arm`), and none at all for 32-bit Linux.",
